&lt;h3&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Senior Research Executive you&#39;ll join the Research Operations &amp;amp; Discovery team, which looks after the research behind GWI Core, our flagship survey of internet users across 50+ markets, and the wider research operations that keep our data accurate, consistent and trusted. Within the Core project team, you&#39;ll own day-to-day delivery of Core research, from questionnaire changes and scripting through fieldwork, quality control and sign-off.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fieldwork is where this role leans most. Core collects responses every day of the year through 20+ sample partners, so you&#39;ll manage live fieldwork across global markets, monitor respondent quality and make the calls that keep collection on time and to standard. Within your first six months, you&#39;ll take ownership of one of Core&#39;s fieldwork studies. You&#39;ll also help shape how Core is built and fielded as it evolves, including more automated and AI-assisted ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few things you&#39;ll be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing multi-market fieldwork with our sample partners: sample and quota set-up, progress tracking, and fast resolution of issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning Core survey updates end to end, from desk research on proposed changes through scripting and quality-checking in Qualtrics and our internal tool (routing and translations included), launch and data checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applying and improving respondent quality and data validation checks, and flagging data quality risks early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with Product, Data and Research so Core changes are documented, clearly specced for our data engineers and reflected accurately across our platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to quota, weighting and fieldwork automation initiatives, and keeping our methodology documentation current&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at GWI means a high tempo environment where change is common. We&#39;re building quickly because the industry is moving quickly, and our customers rely on us to stay ahead. If you like being part of that, you&#39;ll enjoy it here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What do I need to bring with me?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll need to be able to demonstrate the core skills this role requires. You don&#39;t have to tick all the boxes right away; the important thing is that you&#39;re willing to learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial experience in quantitative market research, including writing, scripting and running surveys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing fieldwork with sample or panel providers, ideally across multiple markets (any scale counts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid grasp of survey scripting logic, ideally in Qualtrics or a comparable platform: you can check a script against its questionnaire and spot when routing or logic is off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong grasp of survey methodology (sampling, quotas, weighting, questionnaire design, data quality), with meticulous attention to detail and an eye for anomalies in large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organised, curious and collaborative: you juggle several deadlines, communicate clearly and early, ask why things are done the way they are, and look for ways to do them better, including with automation and AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/em&gt; questionnaire writing or content development for tracking studies, and experience specifying data requirements for a data engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
