&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Programme Lead / Operations Director&lt;/strong&gt; on a 3 month FTC to spearhead a major operational stabilisation and governance programme across one of our flagship global accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead a critical programme to standardise operating models, establish robust commercial and delivery controls, and ensure full operational audit-readiness across creative, media, CX, and technology workstreams. You will bridge senior strategy with hands-on delivery—moving a complex, multi-market operation toward clear, verifiable governance and sustainable ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct the overarching governance and stabilisation programme; own the master roadmap, milestone tracking, and executive governance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational &amp;amp; Commercial Controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with workstream leads across Finance, Operations, Tech, and Commercial to design and embed gate registers, approval frameworks, and compliance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Stakeholder Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive active adoption of standard processes across service towers, regional delivery hubs, and senior client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Tooling Optimisation:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive workflow tool standardisation (including enterprise workflow systems such as Workfront), establishing automated tracking and reporting against contractual SLAs and performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Readiness &amp;amp; Assurance:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead readiness preparations for upcoming corporate and operational audit reviews, coordinating evidence gathering, walk-throughs, and response tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Future Operating Model Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate programme outcomes and proven controls into standard operating procedures (SOPs), role definitions, and a seamless handover to Business-As-Usual (BAU) operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior &amp;amp; Hands-On:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience steering complex programmes with executive stakeholders, paired with the appetite to roll up your sleeves and drive day-to-day execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influential Leader:&lt;/strong&gt; Adept at aligning cross-functional teams—including Delivery, Finance, Tech, Legal, and senior client partners—who do not report to you directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Disciplinary Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable translating between delivery operations, commercial agreements, technology workflows, and contractual governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years within a top-tier agency, management consultancy, or corporate marketing operations environment, leading large-scale operating model transformations, compliance programmes, or audit-readiness initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
