&lt;p&gt;At mthree, we connect talented graduates with top tier organizations, including leading investment banks and companies across insurance, travel, and more. We currently have a Data Engineer role with a leading financial company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Data Engineer to design, build and maintain scalable cloud-native data pipelines that transform data into trusted, AI-ready datasets. The role will focus on data modelling, curation, governance and the delivery of high-quality datasets that support analytics, AI and business decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;London or Glasgow - 5 days onsite&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and maintenance of cloud-based data pipelines using modern data engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the team to ingest, transform and deliver data from a variety of vendor and market data sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and maintain reliable, accurate and accessible datasets for internal users and applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with developing data models and data structures to support new datasets and business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with large datasets and learn how to build solutions that can process and manage data at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the implementation of data quality checks, monitoring and governance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help prepare AI-ready and analytics-ready datasets for use by internal teams and applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve data quality, performance and reliability, working closely with more experienced engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with data engineering, analytics, product and governance teams to understand requirements and deliver data solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and apply best practices in data engineering, cloud technologies and data management as part of the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Data Science, Data Analytics, Computer Science, or a closely related subject.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of data engineering concepts, including data pipelines, data transformation and data management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical and problem-solving skills, with an interest in working with large datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of databases and SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Databricks or Snowflake is highly desirable, but not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a willingness to learn new technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with technical and non-technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any industry placement, internship or project experience in data engineering, data analytics or data science would be an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply&amp;nbsp;via&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;form&amp;nbsp;below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage&amp;nbsp;in&amp;nbsp;video&amp;nbsp;interviews&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;our&amp;nbsp;friendly&amp;nbsp;talent&amp;nbsp;team&amp;nbsp;(30&amp;nbsp;min&amp;nbsp;video&amp;nbsp;call)&lt;/li&gt;
